  "title": "The Trojan War (traditional)",
  "summary": "Greek tradition tells of a ten-year war in which Greek forces besieged Troy in north-western Anatolia, best known from Homer's Iliad. Ancient writers dated it between the 14th and 12th centuries BCE; Eratosthenes' date is 1184 BCE. Historians debate whether any such war happened, though Hittite texts show Greek-Hittite rivalry over a place called Wilusa, identified with Troy.",
